# .gitignore -- commit the recipe, ignore the bulk, keep the manifest.
# See 05-git-and-artifacts.md. This tool has no API-key dotfile: the Canvas
# token is entered interactively and lives only in the running server's
# memory, never in a file, so there is no secrets file to list here.

# Python env / caches / build
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
vendor/testmaker-mcqer/node_modules/

# Generated artifacts: regenerable by re-running the matching *.command
out/
release/

# Instructor-only assessment data. Keep the instructions, never version real
# question sources, answer mappings, generated keys, or Canvas backups.
private/testmaking/*
!private/testmaking/README.md
private/transcripts/
private/redaction/
# Instructor-only integrity-assurance configuration, catchwords, scripts, and
# scan reports. These materials are excluded from GitHub and distributions.
private/integrity-assurance/
# Local instructor command that invokes the private integrity layer.
commands/update-canvas-from-authoring.command

# Raw course-package inputs may contain copyrighted or instructor-only source.
# Commit distributable examples under examples/ after the safety build instead.
input/imscc/*.imscc

# macOS
.DS_Store

# If a future asset directory needs bulk-ignore-but-keep-the-manifest,
# add it here following this pattern:
# assets/<lib>/*
# !assets/<lib>/manifest.json
